cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this manuscript using the metadata below."
title: "Who Is Cloning My Repositories? An Exploration of 598 Daily Clone Events Across Six Public Repositories From Exactly 8,372 Recorded Clone Events ÷ 14 Days—With 0 Visitors, 0 Views, No Referrals, Stars, Forks, or External Public Discussion for DobeWorks and DEGS at the Original Snapshot"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: "McCoy"
    given-names: "Taylor"
date-released: 2026-10-20
version: 1.5.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tmccoy678/Who-is-cloning-my-repos"
abstract: >-
  I investigated exactly 8,372 GitHub-counted clone events across six public
  repositories in a 14-day window, averaging 598 per day. Four repositories
  continued at 568-582 combined clones per day over October 13-19. Reproducible
  R analysis compares observation windows, clone events, daily unique-cloner
  counts, and count rates. A screened external comparison retains 134 series and
  replays all 138 original extracted vectors from pinned public sources. The
  pattern is consistent with recurring automated collection; the operator is
  unknown.
